A MIDI clip's events decided as they play (Segno: docs/design/piano-roll.md §26, ADR 0062).

Notes left to chance roll again each time the song plays and each time the loop comes round, so
what plays can't be decided once, where tracktion builds a clip's sequence. EngineBehaviour::
createMidiPlaybackFilter gives a clip's MidiNode a filter that, on the audio thread, decides each
event it plays by its index in the sequence (and each note it chases when playback starts inside
it): left out, or played with another velocity. Its CombiningNode's view of what's sounding
(addNotesPlayingAt) asks the filter too. With no filter, nothing changes.

